        <div class="explain">
          <div class="ev">
            <span class="mk">How to read this</span>
            <p>Each bar is one fiscal year, April to March. The blue part is UPI, which began in August 2016; the grey part is everything else. The year in progress is left out until its March is in.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="now">
            <span class="mk">As of {lastFy}</span>
            <p>Indians made <b id="ex-an-tot">–</b> payments in {lastFy}, <b id="ex-an-upi">–</b> of them by UPI. In {firstFy} they made <b id="ex-an-tot0">–</b>.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <div class="break">
      <figure id="cb-long" style="margin:0">
        <div class="plate-head">
          <div class="t">
            <h3>Fifteen years before UPI: NEFT and card payments at shops since 2004</h3>
            <div class="sub">Number of payments a month, crore: NEFT, and card payments at shops' card machines (PoS), April 2004 to {PM.long}. Two tables: the RBI's old layout to October 2019 (pale) and the re-organised one from November 2019 (solid), drawn side by side, never joined.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="plate-val"><div class="v acc" id="pv-long">–</div><div class="c">NEFT payments, {PM.long}</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="frame">
          <div class="legend">
            <button class="chip"><i style="background:#2E4BD8"></i>NEFT</button>
            <button class="chip"><i style="background:#5F6675"></i>Card payments at shops (PoS)</button>
          </div>
          <div class="plotzone"><div id="plot-long" style="position:relative"></div></div>
          <div class="plotfoot">
            <span class="src">Source: RBI, Payment System Indicators (DBIE report 612), old layout (lines 4.3, 5.1.2, 5.2.2) and re-organised layout (lines 2.6, 4.1.1, 4.2.1). The old table repeats July 2010 to June 2011 in the rows for August 2006 to July 2007, so that year is left blank.</span>
