          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="explain">
          <div class="ev">
            <span class="mk">How to read this</span>
            <p>The dotted line in November 2019 is where the RBI changed its table, so the lines stop and start again rather than run through. NEFT reads much the same on both sides. Card payments do not: the old table's "usage at PoS" is close to the new table's card payments of every kind, which suggests it also counted online card payments that the new table puts under "others". The RBI does not say, so read the two card stretches as different measures. The jump in card payments late in 2016 is demonetisation, when cash ran short for weeks and shops that had a card machine suddenly used it.</p>
          </div>
