  <footer class="provenance">
    <h2 class="prov-h">Sources, method and revisions</h2>
    <div class="cols">
      <div>
        <h6>Source of record</h6>
        <p>Reserve Bank of India: Payment System Indicators (RBI Bulletin Table 45, monthly, and the Handbook of Statistics on the Indian Economy, yearly), Statistical Tables Relating to Banks in India (Tables 22 and 27) and the Handbook's e₹ table, read from India Atlas's archived copy of the RBI's DBIE database. Currency with the public comes from this site's credit guide. Data vintage <b id="prov-vintage">–</b>.</p>
        <p>Checked against the RBI's own publications: UPI in July 2026 (2,36,583.53 lakh transactions, ₹29,87,880.48 crore) and 2,52,508 ATMs (Bulletin Table 45); UPI in 2024-25 (18,587 crore transactions, RBI Annual Report); e₹ in circulation of ₹1,016.5 crore at end-March 2025 (RBI Annual Report).</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>Method</h6>
        <p>Every DBIE value is printed once per display unit; this guide keeps the actual figures. Averages, shares and growth rates are computed here. Totals are checked against their parts every time the data is rebuilt, the yearly table against the sum of its months, and the RBI's own printed growth rates against growth computed from its levels.</p>
        <p>Two defects in the DBIE export are corrected, both disclosed: the old table's ATM and PoS counts are stored multiplied by ten lakh, and the Handbook's old-layout yearly table is stored at a hundredth of its true values (it is not used; the monthly table covers those years).</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>Revisions and breaks</h6>
        <p>The RBI re-organised its payment table in November 2019; the old layout (April 2004 to October 2019) and the new are separate rulers, never joined. Cheque clearing moved from city clearing houses to three grids and then one national grid, so centre-wise cheque counts stop and start. Recent months may be revised in later Bulletins.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>This guide</h6>
        <p>Version 1.0, built October 2026 from data to {PM.long}. Revised each month when the RBI Bulletin publishes the next month.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
